SUMMARY:Meriem Chabani. Communion It is embarrassing to believe. It is terr
 ifying to care. What happens when we dare anyway?
LOCATION:MIT\, 77 Massachusetts Ave\, Cambridge\, MA 02139
DESCRIPTION:Algerian born\, Paris based Meriem Chabani is the founder and P
 rincipal of NEW SOUTH\, an award-winning architecture\, urban planning and
  anthropology practice that puts the margin at the center. Her work on civ
 ic spaces\, memory and belonging includes the Taungdwingyi cultural center
  in Myanmar\, the Globe Aroma refugee art center in Brussels\, and the upc
 oming Mosque Zero in Paris. She is currently a finalist for the National S
 lavery Museum in Amsterdam. As an educator\, Chabani has taught and lectur
 ed extensively. She has notably served as Aga Khan Design Critic in Archit
 ecture at Harvard GSD (USA)\, and currently teaches at Ecole Paris Malaqua
 is (FR). Her work has regularly been distinguished and showcased at a numb
 er of international architecture Biennials\, including Venice\, Istanbul\,
  Oslo and Lagos. In 2020 Chabani won the Europe 40 under 40 award from The
  European Centre for Architecture and The Chicago Athenaeum. In 2023\, she
  is one of the emerging women architects for AMC. In 2025\, Le Monde names
  her one of the leading voices in culture in France.\nhttps://calendar.mit
 .edu/event/meriem-chabani-communion-it-is-embarrassing-to-believe-it-is-te
 rrifying-to-care-what-happens-when-we-dare-anyway\nFrom Pushpin Boston: ht
 tps://pushpin.city/
URL:https://calendar.mit.edu/event/meriem-chabani-communion-it-is-embarrass
 ing-to-believe-it-is-terrifying-to-care-what-happens-when-we-dare-anyway
END:VEVENT
